  ("Kinematics: Equations of uniformly accelerated motion: v = u + at, s = ut + (1/2)at^2, v^2 = u^2 + 2as. They apply only when acceleration is constant, and s is the signed displacement, not the distance travelled.", "easy", "sign convention"),
  ("Kinematics: Projectile motion: horizontal velocity u cos(theta) stays constant while the vertical motion has acceleration -g. Time of flight T = 2u sin(theta)/g, maximum height H = u^2 sin^2(theta)/(2g), range R = u^2 sin(2theta)/g.", "medium", "formula misapplication"),
  ("Kinematics: Relative velocity: v_AB = v_A - v_B as vectors. In river-boat problems the shortest crossing time is obtained by heading perpendicular to the bank; zero drift needs v_boat sin(theta) = v_river upstream.", "medium", "incomplete case analysis"),
